From 62cd439667f8c110b97ce4b6e1c06e80e25bc44d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:10:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek_v41: four ranks (TP=4) on four DGX Sparks

The family on 2 or 4 ranks (--tp 4 --rank 0..3), opt in per family (CUDA_TP); TP=2 unchanged.

- Whole-128-block uneven splits of the vocabulary, the routed experts and the DSpark delta (weights.block_bounds;
  vocabulary slices 32,384 / 32,384 / 32,256 / 32,256, experts 640 / 640 / 512 / 512 columns).
- Candidates at any count: every rank sends the same k (pick.rank_top: the widest slice's, narrower ones padded
  with -inf / PAD and dropped after the merge), so the all-gather sizes agree past the narrowest slice (top_k above
  32,256, nucleus rows' full vocabulary); the trimmed draft head's lists follow the block split.
- Candidate kernels warmed at boot (cand_warm) and the pinned candidates buffer grown before the forward
  (cand_reserve): the first very wide request after a boot no longer waits on CUDA's lazy module loading or
  cudaHostAlloc inside a window whose Engram gate is waiting for row reads.
- N-way rank agreement (settings, session tier keys, ints), the plan link (TCP: followers say rank and world,
  rank 0 orders and refuses strays; RDMA mailbox at any world size), fail-fast with a channel per follower,
  the memory floor and adaptive prefill reading the tightest follower, image budgets for followers, RoCE post
  rotation over N peers, TF_DSV41_PREFILL_ATTN_BMQ clamped to the heads a rank holds (16 at TP=4).
- The session NVMe tier keys TP=4 separately; TP=2's key is unchanged (saved sessions keep).

tests/test_dsv41_tp4.py (block bounds, slices, TP=4 equals one rank exactly, ranks bit for bit, row invariance,
greedy over the uneven vocabulary, Engram from packed shards) and tests/test_dsv41_four_sparks.py (the review's
bugs, each pinned); tests/dsv41_fakes.py's all-gather refuses unequal sizes like NCCL.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
